                  "engine/settings/merge.go:104",
                  "engine/settings/review_stop_test.go:84"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 9 changed paths in the patch.",
              "The new family reuses the shared hookFamily implementation. Its tests cover entry shape, a never-blocking sh command (missing binary and exit 2 both give exit 0), identity non-overlap, missing/drifted/duplicate reporting, an empty hook command, foreign Stop entry preservation across Install, re-Install and Uninstall, Stop key cleanup, and upgrade of an older install.",
              "The change to removeHooks is scoped: Stop removal goes through the family's own ownership check, so entries from other families and other programs on Stop are kept, and a test pins this.",
              "HasSupportedClaudeLifecycleState now requires the Stop hook, and the lifecycle test adds the families one at a time. This is the requested behavior and not a regression.",
